From 3686cfb94a037e5df2b70d11eab9ed52efa77bfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 15:00:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] sm8850-common: Extract the ShareBuffer allocator
 implementation

libsharebuffer.so lazily dlopens /odm/lib64/libsharebuffer_impl.so and resolves
createShareBufferAllocator from it, so the implementation has to ship.

It must link the platform libui/libutils from /vendor/lib64. sm8850 builds both
from source, so remapping the implementation onto private stock-firmware copies
puts a second instance of each in the process: the allocator is then constructed
against the stock pair while the facade resolves through the source-built pair,
the singleton never holds an AndroidShareBufferAllocator, and
ShareBuffer_CheckBufferPool tail-branches through a vtable slot that does not
exist, crashing the camera app on every mode switch.
---
 proprietary-files.txt | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/proprietary-files.txt b/proprietary-files.txt
index cdd01e1..4806a92 100644
--- a/proprietary-files.txt
+++ b/proprietary-files.txt
@@ -1298,6 +1298,15 @@ vendor/lib64/libwfduibcsrcinterface_vendor.so
 vendor/lib64/libwfdutils_proprietary.so
 vendor/lib64/vendor.qti.hardware.wifidisplaysession_aidl-V1-ndk.so;MODULE_SUFFIX=_vendor
 vendor/lib64/vendor.qti.hardware.wifidisplaysessionl@1.0-halimpl.so
+
+# Camera (Oplus camera port): ShareBuffer allocator, dlopen'd by libsharebuffer.so
+# and resolved via createShareBufferAllocator. It links the platform libui/libutils
+# from /vendor/lib64 - do NOT remap it onto private -stock copies. Doing so puts a
+# second instance of libui/libutils in the process, so the allocator singleton no
+# longer holds an AndroidShareBufferAllocator and ShareBuffer_CheckBufferPool
+# tail-branches through a vtable slot that does not exist.
+odm/lib64/libsharebuffer_impl.so
+
 # Dolby Vision Service
 odm/bin/hw/dvs-aidl-service
 odm/etc/init/dvs-aidl-service.rc
